  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="HH1C967D5CB7055C23C61684D3A8ADDA65" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="HH660FC444EE17A785BFF22BCDC6434313" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4" decimals="0" unitRef="HHferc_us_Pure">2025</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="HHBD1AFC97EAE2BF213BAE5A53CD7CEAC7" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">Q4</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="HH8FD963CECD5B15C379755C94FECA9889" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">2026-04-10</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="HHFF9F4E3640A578CDF5DE55A091A9A0F9" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="HH2FB9527C1D4BB25D79F1C0C76F5BC95D" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="HHDB4E63D65FD21AE5462A8FBA840EA717" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="HH22FBAEA0509E80B804A4341B1670898A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: inherit;"&gt;On July 18, 2018, in Docket No. PL17-1-001, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;Commission&amp;#8221;) dismissed the requests for rehearing and clarification of its revised policy statement on treatment of income taxes (&amp;#8220;Revised Policy Statement&amp;#8221;) and provided guidance regarding the treatment of accumulated deferred income taxes (&amp;#8220;ADIT&amp;#8221;) in light of its revised policy. &lt;em&gt;Inquiry Regarding the Commission&amp;#8217;s Policy for Recovery of Income Tax Costs&lt;/em&gt;, Order on Rehearing of Revised Policy Statement, 164 FERC &amp;#182; 61,030 (Jul. 18, 2018) (&amp;#8220;July 18 Order&amp;#8221;). Pursuant to the guidance provided by the Commission in its July 18 Order, Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast Pipeline, L.L.C., a tax pass-through entity owned in part by Spectra Energy Partners, LP, a master limited partnership, intends to remove any balances recorded in Accounts 190,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: inherit;"&gt;281, 282, and 283 of the Commission&amp;#8217;s Uniform System of Accounts, as well as excess ADIT that has been transferred to Account 254 and deficient ADIT that has been transferred to Account 182.3. Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast Pipeline, L.L.C. has requested approval from the Chief Accountant of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission to implement the accounting entries necessary for removing these balances. Upon receipt of the Chief Accountant&amp;#8217;s approval, Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast Pipeline,L.L.C. will reflect the removal of these balances in the annual and quarterly financing reporting required by Part 260 of the Commission&amp;#8217;s regulations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="HHE60759687E403C6B3DE58B8464A791E0" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;On May 30, 2024, Maritimes, filed a general Natural Gas Act Section 4 rate case, FERC Docket No. RP24-780, reflecting changes in its cost of&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;service based&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;recourse rates and in other rate related tariff provisions applicable to Maritimes&amp;#8217; customers under its&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;various services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;.&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Maritimes,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;requested an effective date for these changes of July 1, 2024. FERC accepted the&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;changes and rate-related tariff changes, subject to the outcome of an evidentiary hearing, and suspended these changes for the&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;maximum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;five-month period&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;permitted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;under the Natural Gas Act. The motion rates and other rate-related tariff changes were placed into effect, subject to refund, on December 1, 2024. Maritimes reached settlement in principle with its customers during the fourth quarter of 2024. On December 31, 2024, Maritimes filed to place into effect the agreed upon settlement rates on January 1, 2025. In Q1 2025, Maritimes filed the Stipulation and Agreement to resolve the case. FERC accepted the Stipulation and Agreement on April 25, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Maritimes continues to&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;operate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;under its settlement rates that went into effect January 1, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 1pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 116%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;a style="text-decoration: none;" href="#index"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; color: #000000;"&gt;122.1 - Schedule - Notes to Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 1pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 47.75pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; padding-right: 31pt; padding-left: 31pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Pipeline,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Notes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;For the Years Ended December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; and 2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 1pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 1pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Summary of Operations &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;The terms "we," "our," "us" and "company" as used in this report refer collectively to Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast Pipeline, L.L.C. (M&amp;amp;N LLC) unless the context suggests otherwise. These terms are used for convenience only and are not intended as a precise description of M&amp;amp;N LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Nature of Operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; M&amp;amp;N LLC owns and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;operates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the United States (U.S.) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;portion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; of the Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast Pipeline, a transmission system extending from producing fields in Nova Scotia through New Brunswick, Maine, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;New Hampshire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; and Massachusetts, where it connects with the existing North American pipeline grid. The U.S. system receives gas supply from reserves located offshore Nova Scotia and onshore New Brunswick through the Canadian portion of the Maritimes &amp;amp; Northeast Pipeline system (Canadian system) and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;regasified&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; liquefied natural gas (LNG, natural gas that has been converted to liquid form) from the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Canaport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; LNG import facility in Saint John, New Brunswick via the Brunswick Pipeline owned by Emera, Inc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Our members are M&amp;amp;N Management Company, LLC (an affiliate of Enbridge), Westcoast Energy (U.S.) LLC (an affiliate of Enbridge), Scotia Power U.S., Ltd. (an affiliate of Emera, Inc.), and Mobil Midstream Natural Gas Investments, Inc. (an affiliate of Exxon Mobil Corporation), which ow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;n 38.77%, 38.76%, 12.92%, and 9.55% &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;interests in us, respectively, at December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; and 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;M&amp;amp;N Management Company, LLC, our managing member, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;is responsible for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the overall development and operation of the U.S. system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Our system is subject to the rules and regulations of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;We &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;own&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; jointly with Portland Natural Gas Transmission System (PNGTS) Phase I and a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;portion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; of Phase II facilities. PNGTS reimburses us for construction costs and operating costs related to its share of the joint facilities. The PNGTS capacity entitlement is part of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;PNGTS&amp;#8217;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; system and is not part of our system. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Accordingly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;, the costs and revenues associated with PNGTS&amp;#8217; capacity are not reflected in our results of operations, financial &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; or cash flows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;2. Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;. The financial statements presented herein have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts (USOA) and published accounting releases which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (U.S. GAAP). Our accounting policies &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;generally conform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; to FERC USOA. The most significant differences between U.S. GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the Comparative Balance Sheet, Statement of Income and the Statement of Cash Flows, (2) accounting for income taxes on a regulatory basis using the stand-alone method of income tax allocation, and 3) cost allocation methodology on central functions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Use of Estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; The preparation of financial statements requires us to make estimates and assumptions that affect the amounts reported in the Financial Statements and Notes to Financial Statements. Although these estimates are based on our best available knowledge at the time, actual results could differ.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Cost-Based Regulation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;We account for our regulated operations &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;under the provisions of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; FERC USOA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-style: italic;"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;The economic effects of regulation can result in a regulated company recording assets for costs that have been or are expected to be approved for recovery from customers or recording liabilities for amounts that are expected to be returned to customers in the rate-setting process in a period different from the period in which the amounts would be recorded by an unregulated enterprise. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Accordingly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;, we record assets and liabilities that result from the regulated ratemaking process that may not be recorded under U.S. GAAP for non-regulated entities. We continually assess whether regulatory assets are probable of future recovery by considering factors such as applicable regulatory changes and recent rate orders applicable to other regulated entities. Based on this assessment, we believe our existing regulatory assets are probable &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; recovery. These regulatory assets and liabilities are classified on the Comparative Balance Sheet as Deferred Debits and Deferred Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue Recognition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; Revenues from the transportation of natural gas are recognized when the service is provided. Revenues related to these services provided but not yet billed are estimated each month. These estimates are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;generally based&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; on contract data, regulatory information, and preliminary throughput and allocation measurements. Final bills for the current month are billed and collected in the following month. Differences between actual and estimated revenues are immaterial. We also have certain customer contracts with billed amounts that decline annually over the terms of the contract. Differences between the amounts billed and recognized are deferred &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the Comparative Balance Sheet. See Note 4 for further discussion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;. Income taxes have been historically recorded &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;in accordance with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; the FERC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances issued in 1995 in Docket No. PL05-5, which &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;permitted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity. Income taxes are continuing to be recorded in this manner &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;in light of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the purchase by Spectra Energy &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Corp, a corporate subsidiary of Enbridge Inc., in December 2018, of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;all of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the outstanding &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;publicly-traded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; units of Spectra Energy Partners, LP (&amp;#8220;SEP&amp;#8221;), our immediate parent company. Deferred income taxes are recognized for differences between the financial reporting and tax bases of assets and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;liabilities at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; enacted statutory tax rates in effect for the years in which the differences are expected to reverse. Actual income taxes could vary from these estimates due to future changes in income tax law or results from the final review of tax returns by federal or state tax authorities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;On March 15, 2018, in Docket No. PL17-1-000, the FERC changed its long-standing policy on the treatment of income tax included in the rates of pipelines and other entities subject to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;cost of service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; rate regulation within a Master Limited Partnership (MLP). In its order, the FERC revised its policy in Docket No. PL05-5, and stated that its policy was to no longer permit entities organized as an MLP to recover an income tax allowance in their cost of service rates on the basis that investor-level income tax costs are reflect in an MLP pipeline&amp;#8217;s cost of service through the return on equity rate base. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;On July 18, 2018, the FERC issued an Order in Docket No. PL17-1-001, that: (1) dismissed all requests for rehearing of its March 15, 2018 revised policy statement on the treatment of income tax costs and explained that its revised policy statement does not establish a binding rule, but is instead an expression of general policy that the Commission intends to follow in the future; and (2) provides guidance that because an MLP pipeline&amp;#8217;s cost of service no longer includes income tax costs in the form of an income tax allowance pursuant to FERC&amp;#8217;s Revised Policy Statement, then the MLP pipeline may remove Accumulated Deferred Income Tax (ADIT) balances from its Part 201 (18 C.F.R. Part 201) books and any related regulatory assets or regulatory liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;On September 10, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;2018&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; in accordance with FERC accounting regulations, 18 C.F.R. Part 201, and FERC&amp;#8217;s July 18, 2018 Order in Docket No. PL17-1-001, SEP, on behalf of certain of its pipeline affiliates, including M&amp;amp;N LLC, requested approval from the FERC Chief Accountant of accounting entries eliminating deferred tax balances and excess deferred tax balances. This request is pending in Docket No. AC18-220-000. We will make all necessary adjustments to account balances based upon the outcome in Docket No. AC18-220-000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;On November 27, 2023, SEP, a subsidiary of Enbridge Inc., filed with the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) in Docket No. AC18-220-000 a request on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;behalf of certain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; of SEP&amp;#8217;s pipeline and affiliates, including MNLLC, for a Motion for Action on its September 10, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;2018&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; request for approval of accounting entries in this proceeding. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Cash. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Cash includes cash on hand and amounts deposited in accounts with a US chartered bank and is recorded at cost which approximates fair value. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Accumulated Provision for Uncollectible Accounts - Credit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; Accounts &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;receivable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; are measured at cost. For accounts receivable, a loss allowance matrix is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;utilized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; to measure lifetime expected credit losses. The matrix contemplates historical credit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;losses by age of receivables, adjusted for any forward-looking information and management expectations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Plant Materials and Operating Supplies. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Other materials and supplies are recorded using average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Natural Gas Imbalances. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;The Comparative Balance Sheet includes in-kind balances &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;as a result of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; differences in gas volumes received and delivered &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Since settlement of certain imbalances is in-kind, changes in their balances do not &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;have an effect on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; our Statement of Cash Flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;Natural gas volumes owed to or by us are valued at natural gas market index prices as of the balance sheet dates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;Utility Plant. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;Utility Plant is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;stated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; at historical &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; less accumulated depreciation. We capitalize all construction-related direct labor and material costs, as well as indirect construction costs. Indirect costs include general engineering, taxes, and the cost of funds used during construction. The costs of renewals and betterments that extend the useful life or increase the expected output of utility &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; are also capitalized. The costs of repairs, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;replacements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; and major maintenance projects, that do not extend the useful life or increase the expected output of utility &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;, are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;expensed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; as incurred. Depreciation is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;generally computed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; over the asset&amp;#8217;s estimated useful life using the straight-line method. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Depreciation is recorded using the group method of depreciation which is commonly used by pipelines, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;utilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; and similar entities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;See also &amp;#8220;Allowance f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;or Funds Used During Construction (AFUDC)&amp;#8221; discussed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;below&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Allowance &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; Funds Used During Construction (AFUDC). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;AFUDC, which &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;represents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the estimated debt and equity costs of capital funds necessary to finance the construction of certain new regulated facilities, consists of two components, an equity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; and an interest expense &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;. The equity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; is a non-cash item. After construction is completed, we are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;permitted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; to recover these costs through inclusion in the rate base and in the depreciation provision. AFUDC is capitalized as a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; of Total Utility Plant cost, with offsetting credits to the Statements of Income through Other Income and Deductions for the equity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; and Interest Charges for the interest expense &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Preliminary Project Costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; Project development costs, including expenditures for preliminary surveys, plans, investigations, environmental studies, regulatory applications and other costs incurred for the purpose of determining the feasibility of capital expansion projects, are capitalized for rate-regulated enterprises when it is determined that recovery of such costs through regulated revenues of the completed project is probable. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Long-Lived Asset Impairment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;We evaluate assets for impairment when events or circumstances &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;indicate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; that the carrying value may not be recovered. These events include market declines that are believed to be other than temporary, changes in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;manner in which&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; we intend to use a long-lived asset and adverse changes in the legal or business environment, such as adverse actions by regulators. When an event occurs, we evaluate the recoverability of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;its&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; carrying value based on its long-lived &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;assets&amp;#8217; ability to generate future cash flows on an undiscounted basis. If impairment is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;indicated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;, for purposes of USOA, we will adjust the carrying value of assets downward to fair value after seeking governmental approval or have the option to file a rate case.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations (AROs). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Asset retirement obligations (ARO) associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recognized and measured at fair value in the period in which they can be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;reasonably determined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;. Fair value approximates the cost a third party would charge to perform the tasks necessary to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;retire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; such assets and is recognized at the present value of expected future cash flows. ARO is added to the carrying value of the associated asset and depreciated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;over&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; the asset's useful life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Currently, it is not possible to make a reasonable estimate of ARO due to the indeterminate timing and scope of the asset retirements. These assets include pipelines whose retirement dates will depend mostly on the various natural gas supply sources that connect to our systems and the ongoing demand for natural gas usage in the markets we serve. We expect these supply sources and market demands to continue for the foreseeable &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;future,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; therefore we are unable to estimate retirement dates that would result in ARO liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.5pt; margin-right: 6.9pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Commitments, Contingencies and Environmental Liabilities Expenditures. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Liabilities for other commitments and contingencies are recognized when, after fully analyzing available information, we &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;determine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; it is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; either probable that an asset has been impaired, or a liability has been incurred, and the amount of the impairment or loss can be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;reasonably estimated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;. When a range of probable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;loss&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;can&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;be&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;estimated,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;we&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;recognize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;most&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;likely&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;amount,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;no&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;more&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;likely&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;than another, the minimum of the range of probable loss is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;accrued&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;. We expense legal costs associated with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;loss&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; contingencies as such costs are incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;We expense or capitalize, as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;appropriate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;, expenditures for ongoing compliance with environmental regulations that relate to past or current operations. We expense costs incurred for remediation of existing environmental contamination caused by past operations that do not &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;benefit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; future periods by preventing or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;eliminating&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; future contamination. We record liabilities for environmental matters when assessments &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;indicate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; that remediation efforts are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;probable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; and the costs can be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;reasonably estimated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;. Estimates of environmental liabilities are based on currently available facts,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;3. Changes to Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Adoption of New Accounting Standards. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;The following new Accounting Standards Update (ASUs) was adopted during 2025 and the effects of such adoption, if any, are presented in the accompanying Financial Statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-style: italic;"&gt;Income Tax Disclosures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;Effective January 1, 2025, we adopted ASU 2023-09 on a prospective basis. The new standard was issued in December 2023 with the intent of simplifying &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;the accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; for income taxes. The accounting update removes certain exceptions to the general principles in ASC 740 Income Taxes as well as provides simplification by clarifying and amending existing guidance. The adoption of this ASU did not have a material impact on our financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Future Accounting Policy Changes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-style: italic;"&gt;Measurement of Credit Losses for Accounts Receivable and Contract Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;ASU 2025-05 was issued in July 2025 to address challenges in applying the guidance in Topic 326, Financial Instruments - Credit Losses, to current accounts receivable and current contract assets arising from transactions accounted for under Topic 606, Revenue from Contracts with Customers. The amendment in the update will allow entities to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;elect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; a practical expedient to estimate expected credit losses, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;assuming that&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; current conditions as of the balance sheet date will not change for the remaining life of the related asset. ASU 2025-05 is effective January 1, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; for annual and interim reporting periods and should be applied prospectively. The adoption of this accounting update is not expected to have a material impact on our &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;consolidated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue from Contracts with Customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Major Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;All operating revenues for the year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; ended December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;, and 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt; were earned from contracts with customers for the transportation of natural gas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
